From 48469f6b6b64e1d9ab559338b0cffd1486e5e77d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John <john.de.kroon@cyberant.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:51:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] badgeui: dumps the client saves itself go to Cards
 (iCLASS)

An iCLASS dump runs as a typed Console command (hf iclass dump --ki 0);
the client saved hf-iclass-<CSN>-dump.bin in ~/.proxmark3/dumps, but only
the app's own MIFARE Classic dump wrote cards.tsv, so the dump never showed
under Cards. After every Console or action command the app now reads the
client's "Saved ... to binary file `...`" lines and puts an hf-<type>-<UID>-dump
file (iclass, mf, mfu, 15) on the card: the one searched last when the UID
matches, else a card made from the file name.

The card screen shows an iCLASS dump as 8-byte blocks (CSN, config,
e-purse, Kd, Kc, AIA, then the application) and other dumps as 16-byte
rows; the triangle loads iCLASS with hf iclass eload, Simulate types
hf iclass sim -t 3, Write types hf iclass restore --first 6 --last N --ki 0.
Keys is only offered for MIFARE Classic.

Tested: test_pm3ui.py 12/12 on the host (new test_iclass_dump_to_cards,
with the sim printing the client's colour codes around the path); the
screen compared by eye; cross-build in the VM clean. Not yet on the badge.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
